  "assessment": "Reconciled fourteen direct interests, three stable majors, twenty-four curricular topics, four illustrations and six outcomes. Eleven generators belong to the broad/urban closest core; three each substantiate cultural/identity and social-risk directions. All generator ownership is explicit; removed career-outcome row 9633 from academic-research support, retaining it as search-only. No residual omnibus cluster or inherited split-target evidence is used.",
  "sourceSupport": {
    "9587–9603": "The current programme, three major descriptions and adopted major lists substantiate social relations/cohesion/change, urban inequality/exclusion/welfare, empirical research, family/culture/migration and climate/health/social risks. The major alternatives are interests rather than three simultaneous components of the comparator.",
    "9604–9627": "Named introductory, theoretical, political/social-psychological, qualitative/causal/survey, philosophical and project courses corroborate the support-only topics. The actual Life Course course is health-focused, and the second-year project/thesis use major-specific variants.",
    "9628–9631": "City poverty, comparative cultural identities, cultural climate analysis and welfare exclusion remain illustrations, not additional mandatory subjects or generators.",
    "9632–9637": "Policy, municipal, research, education/welfare, consultancy and postgraduate outcomes remain search-only or conditional; no admission, employment or professional-status guarantee is made."
